      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-30T22:01:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought about it, but I didn\u0027t think that the chip-specific code needed to be aware of board specific device state. Maybe I should move the disabling of the UART to the board specific code.\n\nIf a servoflex was attached, there\u0027d be no reason to bitbang since the FTDI chips on the servo board would be used instead.",
      "parentUuid": "391e3af9_0409fd97",
      "revId": "7ce3c978fe25af3937c6cb077ee4d12ec9beaa17",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
